{
	...
	// uses "m_fmt_buf"?
}
```

I genuinely am not certain whether it's single-buffered or rotating. There IS a documented warning on the AMXX forum by developers: "fmt() uses a single buffer; calling fmt() twice in the same statement will result in the first call's result being overwritten" — hmm, or the opposite, that they made it rotate specifically to allow this.

Given this is a code review and I shouldn't overstate, I'll flag it as: "потенциальная перезапись буфера fmt — две fmt() в одном вызове; поведение зависит от реализации буфера fmt в сборке; безопаснее форматировать в локальные переменные". And I can note: to be definitive, check `fmt` in the headers / test. Per AGENTS.md rule 5: "Не выдавать чтение кода за проверку на живом сервере" — I'll be explicit that this is an analysis-based risk, not a measured fact.

