Then I'll write the review. The review should be structured per problem with: 1) what's wrong, 2) why, 3) severity.

Let me prioritize the most real, high-value findings:

A. **Vault never opened (no nvault_open)** — critical. Every nvault_get/nvault_set runs with handle 0 → native error / wrong vault. Stats are never actually stored/read. Also no nvault_close — but per storage skill, module flushes on map change, so close isn't strictly needed; the missing open is fatal.

B. **Key is userid instead of SteamID** — high. Stats don't survive reconnect; vault grows unboundedly with one entry per connection; after server restart, userids restart and a different player can inherit another player's stats (cross-contamination).

C. **`FinalizeRound()` inside the player loop** — called 32× per round end instead of once. If it mutates stats/round totals, they're applied 32 times. High (or medium-high, depends on undefined function).

